welcome to the first cloud lapse episode  on the gcpd central quest on quick labs  creating a virtual machine in this quest  you get your first hands-on experience  with google cloud get comfortable with  the basics like spinning up a VM and  configuring key infrastructure tools  through working with more advanced  stacked driver and cuber Nettie's  concepts you will work your way through  each lab on quick laps until you have  completed your quest and receive your  badge you do not need a Google cloud  platform account or project an account  project and associated resources are  provided to you as part of each lab  let's see what this lab is about then  Google compute engine lets you create  virtual machines running different  operating systems including multiple  flavors of Linux Debian Ubuntu Red Hat  and core OS and windows server on Google  infrastructure you can run thousands of  virtual CPUs on a system that has been  designed to be fast and to offer strong  consistency of performance in this  hands-on lab you'll learn how to create  virtual machine instance using the  Google cloud platform console and using  the G cloud command line create a  virtual machine with the g-cloud command  line deploy a web server and connect it  to a virtual machine it's helpful if you  have familiarity with standard Linux  text editors such as vim Emacs or Nano  Google compute engine is the foundation  to Google cloud platforms infrastructure  as a service next up on our quest is  compute engine QuickStart windows a  quest is a series of related labs that  form a learning path on quick laps  completing this quest earns you this  badge to recognize your achievement good  luck and have fun  [Music]
 

